---
import ChapterLayout from '../../../layouts/ChapterLayout.astro';
import { getDrakeChapter } from '../../../data/story/drakeChaptersData';
import { processDrakeContentHtml } from '../../../utils/drakeContentProcessor';

const chapter = getDrakeChapter('012-treachery', 'chapter-4')!;

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')
  ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL
  : `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/`;

const rawContentHtml = "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Chapter 4 - And now for a more personal story arc.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Stay_Away_From_The_Summoner.21\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Stay_Away_From_The_Summoner!\">Stay Away From The Summoner!</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Stay Away From The Summoner!\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_4?action=edit&amp;section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: Stay Away From The Summoner!\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Another new character.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>PLAYABLE CHARACTER - <b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Yuna_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Yuna (Dissidia PSP)\">Yuna</a></b>\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-left\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/71/Yuna.png/revision/latest?cb=20210530025542\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Yuna\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/71/Yuna.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/72?cb=20210530025542\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"72\" height=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"Yuna.png\" data-image-key=\"Yuna.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Howdy Yuna, what's shaking?. Yuna isn't my favorite character, but she's certainly not on my list of dislikes. She's got a good character arc in her base game, isn't too annoying (though that may be because Wakka raised the bar for shithead-ery), and is a Summoner, and Summoners are up there as one of my fav character classes. Sure, she's no Rydia or Garnet, but them's some tough competition for anyone. In this game among the six heroes, Yuna is pretty bland though, between Laguna and Vaan being comic relief and Kain and Lightning being stoic badasses, Yuna is just sort of there. In this chapter she gets a much more personal quest than the rest of the group, and in terms of the singular stories of the chapters, I would say it has the best one, and connects very nicely to the 13th cycle. But that's for another part in the future.\n</p><p>In battle, Yuna doesn't fight herself, she calls Aeons to attack for her. And to my great disappointment, it is nowhere near as badass as I'd expect from a Summoner. Yuna has only six Bravery attacks, and they're divided up the same way for ground and air - close-range melee attack, charging mid-range attack, and long-range projectile attack. I find thus that she's very boring to play as, her moves are good for sure, they pack a fair punch, especially in EX Mode, but when there's only four worth using since the projectile attacks suck, it doesn't make for engaging and fun combat. And since she's just starting out she won't learn those charging attacks for several levels, making fighting as her even more boring because she now has basically only two attacks. She does have one combo using the <a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Holy_glitch\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Holy glitch\">Holy glitch</a> - fire off a charge Impulse, and if she recovers before it hits, time your usage of Heavenly Strike as the opponent is hit by Impulse, and even though you didn't hit with Heavenly Strike, the game will let you combo it due to the glitch since Impulse hit. You can practice this throughout the story if you like.\n</p><p>Her HP attacks are better varied, Yuna is an AI Breaker, the computer opponents even in the hardest areas of the game seem incapable of dodging Energy Ray, and Thor's Hammer and Hellfire are nice close-range moves with good radius. Eventually Yuna gets Mega Flare which breaks the AI even harder. And...that's it. Yuna only has two moves worth using until she gets Sonic Wings at Level 12, so run up to an enemy, slam them with Meteor Strike or Heavenly Strike until you can kill them, then fire off an Energy Ray and do so. Nothing else to say, she really can't do anything else yet, and even later there's not much more to it. I have no idea why they made her so limited, FFX had plenty of Aeons and that means Yuna has plenty of potential attacks since she uses the Aeon's moves, so where are Yojimbo and Anima?\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Before we begin, I confess I did a few Sephiroth vs Kefka matches in Quick Battle to get enough Harlequin's Dreams to get a Sunrise. I only did this though because the game's natural story encounters allows enough to get one by this point, I was just unlucky, that's the only \"cheating\" I'm doing though, I'm not gonna go fighting Garlands to get a Hyper Ring because the story hasn't given us enough False Stalwarts to fight for the same yet. I used Sephiroth because we use him in a Report later so he can use the levels, and as a villain it won't skew the difficulty in any later storylines because he won't be used in any. My equipment set-up for now thus is a Power Ring and Sunrise with the Level 1-9 Booster, and the Red Drop because I had a spare Rosetta Stone from last time. You'll also notice as a nod to X-2, Yuna can equip guns. That Valiant is perfect for her, and next chapter when we go back to Lightning, she can use it too. In fact of the six heroes of this storyline, four use guns, and of the two that don't one isn't playable in the last chapters, so guns are pretty much the go-to weapon to prioritize getting since almost everyone can use the guns you buy.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Phantom\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Phantom\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Cotton Robes\"><img alt=\"Cotton Robes\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/df/Dissicon_ff10_Jec3.png/revision/latest?cb=20110120053332\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Assist - Jecht\"><img alt=\"Assist - Jecht\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"34\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"Dissicon ff10 Jec3.png\" data-image-key=\"Dissicon_ff10_Jec3.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/d/df/Dissicon_ff10_Jec3.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/34?cb=20110120053332\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">3\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Imitation Despot\"><img alt=\"Imitation Despot\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Guard Ring\"><img alt=\"Guard Ring\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">4\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235357\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Delusory Dragoon\"><img alt=\"Delusory Dragoon\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"33\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Hard Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/5/58/DFF_Hard_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/33?cb=20110203235357\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234631\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Hairband\"><img alt=\"Hairband\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"30\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chest.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chest.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/3/38/DFF_Chest.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/40?cb=20110203234631\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>As you can tell clearly, a Straight Chain will chain the four enemies here, if you have one. Jecht is our Assist and he's one of the best Assists in the game, his aerial Assist does high damage and slams the opponent into the ground, and it's long enough that if you're close-enough to the opponent when he starts it up, you can hit with Heavenly Strike and recover in time to use Thor's Hammer on the enemy before they recover. His ground Assist is less useful since it slams the opponent up into the air, but a well-timed Heavenly Strike will drive them back down,and depending on the arena they may not be so high as to be unreachable. Also, for most of this storyline we have a lot of new opponents! Let's do a rundown.\n</p><p>The Ephemeral Phantom is Jecht's Manikin, it uses Jecht's ground combo attack Jecht Rush, the midair Jecht Blade which is a charging series of sword swings, and Jecht Block which deflects all moves. Yuna will stagger if he deflects Meteor Strike, but her other moves either cause no stagger or stagger him too, so rely on aerial strikes to fight him. There's an Imitation Despot which you'll recognize from a Report, they have Land Mine which puts so mines on the ground, Meteor Strike will dispel them, and Light Crest which creates an energy field that fires projectiles that bounce off obstacles when you get close. HP is the aerial Flare. The Ephemeral Summoner has the same Meteor Strike and Heavenly Strike as you do, but a Diamond Dust HP attack in the air which has shorter range than Thor's Hammer but executes a lot faster and is hard to anticipate, so be on your toes or only strike when she's grounded. And then there's a Delusory Dragon....you know them by now I'm sure.\n</p><p>And to cover it because hey, this is a guide, the enemies of course have new Battlegen items to win. The White Cape, which gives a magic defense bonus, might want it sometime, can be traded for three Magicite Shards, three Despot's Hopes, and three Flash's Hopes. If you got lucky enough in Chapter 2 to get some Girl's Dreams, the Silver Hourglass which increases EX Mode Duration by 5% needs three Girl's Dreams, three Phantom's Dreams, and three Blackcrystal Slivers, we've got plenty of the last one, since it seems every other battle so far has been in the Chaos Shrine. There's nothing else of note though, still a lot of items needing Battlegen stuff we can't get yet.\n</p><p>The chests have the Cotton Robes and Hairband for equipment, and a Guard Ring, a nice accessory but not anything we need, I prioritize power in my builds. As we leave, Jecht suddenly vanishes and Yuna finds herself alone. Thinking back on something from home, she whistles, and suddenly and impossibly, Tidus comes running by! She calls out to him but Tidus doesn't recognize her and runs off. Time to get to the bottom of this mystery.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_Pilgrimage\">The Pilgrimage</span><a title=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Pilgrimage\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Walkthrough:Dissidia_012_Final_Fantasy/Drake/Part_4?action=edit&amp;section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section&#39;s source code: The Pilgrimage\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the world map we start on a beach (nice mythology gag) and the path forward out into the marshlands is linear. As you come out and grab the second orb of the dead, make a left to a chest with an EX Charge and a Counterfeit Wraith to fight, she has Anti-Air Particle Beam. Continue across the marsh to a ruined castle with a Moogle shop. On my game I had 195 KP, <i>almost</i> enough to get my hands on those coveted 200 KP items! If you have enough now, maybe it's your Bonus Day and you've got a discount or had a Chain Skill I lacked and didn't have to buy one, if you have 200 KP and feel the natural urge to splurge, buy the Icebrand, as Swords are one the most versatile equipment types, usable by a good portion of the hero characters, and the Icebrand is the most powerful sword we can use until we get to Level 30. Vaan, Laguna, Lightning and Kain use Swords, so this weapon will see more than its share of usable throughout the rest of the game, probably going to end up being used by all my characters throughout the 013 story except for Terra since she can't use swords (I don't know why, she could in FF6, but that's not something we need to get into here).\n</p><p>For the other items available, none of them are must-buy items, but Empty Assist Gauge would be the best if you must, since the other four have fluctuating activation requirements, EAG, you'll always know when you have no Assist and thus the gauge will always be empty during that time. As an edit note, while writing this walkthrough I did not buy EAG and later wished I had, so yes, buy it, learn from my mistakes. Summons are all a waste of KP at this point. Buy a Multichain for down the road, we may get one from the orbs of the dead but it's unlikely. The stone produces a grind bar leading to a Rosetta Stone. As we approach the next gateway you'll see Tidus turn and run behind it.\n</p>\n<table class=\"D012 board\" style=\"float:right\">\n\n<tbody><tr bgcolor=\"068FB0\">\n<td width=\"19px;background:white\">&#160;\n</td>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">A\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">B\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">C\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">D\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">E\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">F\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">G\n</th>\n<th style=\"width:40px\">H\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">1\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest?cb=20141117182922\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Stigma of Chaos\"><img alt=\"Stigma of Chaos\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"39\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Stigma Of Chaos.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/73/DFF_Stigma_Of_Chaos.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/39?cb=20141117182922\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">2\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; tex