w-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Summoner\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235702\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"The Emperor\"><img alt=\"The Emperor\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"36\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Chaos Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Chaos_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/86/DFF_Chaos_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/36?cb=20110203235702\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">5\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203235732\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Potion\"><img alt=\"Potion\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"21\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Potion.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Potion.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/f/fc/DFF_Potion.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/21?cb=20110203235732\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"Ephemeral Phantom\"><img alt=\"Ephemeral Phantom\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">6\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"DFF Start\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Start.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Start.png\" data-relevant=\"0\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/7/7a/DFF_Start.png/revision/latest?cb=20201209045748\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\">&#160;\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr>\n<tr style=\"height:40px; text-align:center\">\n<th bgcolor=\"068FB0\">7\n</th>\n<th bgcolor=\"cabd62\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest?cb=20110203234241\" class=\"mw-file-description image\" title=\"False Hero\"><img alt=\"False Hero\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"16\" height=\"40\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"DFF Battle Piece.png\" data-image-key=\"DFF_Battle_Piece.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/b/b5/DFF_Battle_Piece.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/16?cb=20110203234241\" /></a></span>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th>\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th>\n<th style=\"display:none\">\n</th></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>There's a lot of enemies here but don't be intimidated, we can handle them. First fight the Imitation Despot at D4, then move there and use a Multichain to chain six enemies and win a lot of KP. Feel free to use that EX Charge and take damage in the fights, that Potion there will let us fill our HP and EX to full before we face the boss. Speaking of EX Mode, time to chat about that I guess. Yuna's EX Mode increases her damage output to insane levels, when she uses a Bravery attack two Aeons appear to attack at once. Her EX Burst has commands appear as rings of light close around them, press the shown command just as the ring closes to be just around the command icon, repeat several times. During this round of enemies Yuna got to Level 11 and learned a new HP attack along the way up, Hellfire. It creates three columns of flame in front of her with a pretty high reach, it's effective at close-range and can deflect those attacks like Flare and Windburst on start-up, but otherwise stick with Energy Ray.\n</p><p>The enemies are two Ephemeral Phantoms, two Ephemeral Visions, two False Heroes, an Imitation Despot, and an Ephemeral Summoner, all enemies you've seen before and can handle. The Phantoms have Triumphant Grasp, a downward-arcing charge HP attack that can easily be avoided by just getting above them, and the Visions have Energy Rain. One of them is the Strange Battle Piece and has Odin along with 3000 starting Bravery. Cactuar is good if you have charges for it. The False Heroes have an HP attack called Radiant Sword, it creates six swords of light that fire outwards and spread out, then turn and rush you to impale you. It can't be blocked and the swords will deflect your projectiles, so you'll have to dodge them. They have quite a bit of range on them too. As I said, if you take an HP hit or two, it's fine.\n</p><p>The chests have a Pink Tail (that's six) and a Soul of Valor. Chug the Potion and approach the Chaos Piece. Yuna finds Jecht and Tidus squaring off and intervenes. Seems the Warriors of Chaos got Tidus here to take down Jecht and have brainwashed him. Ya know, if you wanted to recruit characters to take out Jecht, why on earth would you go for Tidus? I guess it makes sense, he did kill Jecht once already, but he sort of had help. Now Hades, there was a man with taste in minions, why settle for the rest when you can have Auron? Yuna tries to get through to Tidus, encouraging him to remember her and Jecht, and Tidus seems to begin to wake up when the Emperor appears and launches off a Flare at Yuna. Tidus takes the hit and gets blasted, and the Emperor sneers down at Yuna for screwing up the fight he had set up. Yuna orders Jecht to take care of Tidus while she handles the Emperor. Gotta admire her guts, she tells <i>Jecht</i> to stay back.\n</p>\n<table style=\"width: 275px; D012 article-table; text-align: center; color:black; float:right\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"font-size: larger; background:#1E90FF\" colspan=\"6\"><font color=\"white\"><b>Boss</b></font>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Emperor_Mateus_(Dissidia_PSP)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Emperor Mateus (Dissidia PSP)\">The Emperor</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\" colspan=\"6\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/88/EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest?cb=20110216231129\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"EmperorDissidiaRender\"  decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"91\" height=\"150\" class=\"mw-file-element lazyload\" data-image-name=\"EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-image-key=\"EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG\" data-relevant=\"1\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/finalfantasy/images/8/88/EmperorDissidiaRender.PNG/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/91?cb=20110216231129\" /></a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>HP</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Level</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" colspan=\"2\"><b>Bravery</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"2\">3,270\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">18\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\">299\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>Brave Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Landmine, Thunder Crest, Light Crest, Mine, Dynamite\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"6\"><b>HP Attacks</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"6\">Flare, Starfall\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#1E90FF\">\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Summon</b>\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><b>Difficulty</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr bgcolor=\"#dddddd\">\n<td colspan=\"3\">Giant of Babil\n</td>\n<td colspan=\"3\">2.5/5\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Well as the choice of boss music will remind us, Yuna has experience taking out smug fashion victim mages who won't stay dead. You've already seen most of the Emperor's moves before with the Imitation Despots, but he's smarter about using them - if he snares you in a Thunder Crest, he will take advantage of your vulnerability. To refresh your memory further - Dynamite fires an orb that sticks to obstacles and draws you in to stun you, Thunder Crest creates a lightning field on the ground to do the same, Landmine and Mine toss out exploding orbs of lightning that can be dispelled by dashing through them, and Light Crest creates a field that shoots projectiles when you get close. His new Bravery attack Bombard is a close-range staff smack that knocks you back, but you should never be close enough when he's not being hit himself that it can hit you. He has both versions of Flare, the ground one that follows you and the midair one that stays in place. There's a way to deal with the blue Flare now, lure it into tracking you through a floor or wall, like the giant sword in the middle of the stage or the railings along the edges, and it'll explode when it hits the obstacle. The explosion can still hit you though so stand clear.\n</p><p>His new HP move is Starfall. When he begins to charge it up it has one of the largest charge times in the game, several seconds, but when it goes off you're screwed, a giant meteor is going to slam down on your head preceded by fireballs, and unless you can quickmove away, you are not going to be avoiding it. When charging he's immune to projectile attacks, and unfortunately, Heavenly Strike, strictly speaking, has the same damage priority as a projectile, so the only way to break through his defenses and stop him when he begins Starfall is to use Thor's Hammer or an EX Mode Heavenly Strike, which also calls Ifrit to do a different type of damage that will hit fine. And to wrap up this description, he has the Giant of Babil summon, which saps 30% of your Bravery and his and adds it to the stage pool, and he has accessories for a 10% buff to his magic damage when he's far enough away from you.\n</p><p>With his high defense (for this point), your Bravery attacks won't do as much damage as you're use to, so use Yuna's EX Mode buffs, or Heavenly Strike to knock him down in the banish trap over and over and whittle him down. He can be surprisingly tough, with that HP he can endure two Break-boosted HP attacks and keep coming, and his high level means he'll have a base Bravery boost to over 400 points, so Yuna's 2000 or so HP will melt off pretty quick, especially since his aerial Flare inflicts wall rush. His weakness is fortunately he isn't <i>that</i> smart about using his traps, just smarter than the Manikins, if he played like a human player - that is, Thunder Crest and Flare the place up constantly to keep you from getting close to him - he'd be a real challenge. He still is, for a new player at least, but only because his higher level gives him a power bonus. You can win as long as you aren't stupid and don't blunder into his traps too much.\n</p><p>In the aftermath of the fight, the Emperor observes Tidus and Jecht laying unconscious, and notices Jecht transferred his power to Tidus to save his life at seemingly the cost of his own. Deciding to use this to his advantage, he takes Jecht's shell of a body away and vanishes, leaving Tidus to Yuna. Laguna and Vaan show up and head off again. We unlock a new Report as always, but this one has no fights and is just a cutscene so I'll let you watch it without summing it up. When we open the menu we'll also be notified that we get a new accessory for completing Chapter 4, the booster Level 10-19, it's also a 1.5 and guess when it activates. Makes an easy and quick replacement for Level 1-9 when you outgrow it. Sadly, the boosters for higher level ranges are only 1.2, but for now these two are great.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<table class=\"toccolours\" width=\"85%\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; margin:0 auto; text-align: center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: center; border:solid 1px\"><b><a href=\"/story/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake\">Drake Clawfang's Dissidia 012 Walkthrough</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"10%\" style=\"border:solid 1px\" rowspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">Previous page</a></b>\n</td>\n<td>\n<table width=\"100%\" style=\"text-align:center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Treachery_of_the_Gods\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Treachery of the Gods\">Treachery of the Gods</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/012-treachery/prologue-chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 1\">Prologue / Chapter 1</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-2/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 2\">2</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-3/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 3\">3</a> - <strong class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</strong> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-5/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 5\">5</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-6/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 6\">6</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/chapter-7/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 7\">7</a> - <a href=\"/story/012-treachery/epilogue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 8\">Epilogue</a><hr />\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b><a href=\"https://finalfantasy.fandom.com/wiki/Light_to_All\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" title=\"Light to All\">Light to All</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/story/013-light/prologue/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 9\">Prologue</a> - <a href=\"/story/013-light/chapter-1/\" title=\"Walkthrough:Dissidia 012 Final Fantasy/Drake/Part 10\">Chapter 1</a> - <a hre